  "notes": "Part 4/5 of Roopkund Lake, continuing directly from Part 3's cliffhanger ('that tidy answer was about to be tested'). Delivers the 2019 Harney et al. DNA reveal: three genetically distinct groups (23 South Asian ancestry, 14 eastern Mediterranean/Crete-related, 1 Southeast Asian) who died in two events roughly 1,000 years apart (7th-10th c. CE vs 17th-20th c. CE). EDITORIAL RULE (all 5 parts, same as Parts 1-3 and Dyatlov Pass): no AI-generated likeness of any real named person or theorized/legendary figure presented as a documented portrait. This part goes further -- group-a/group-b/group-c beats show landscape/place imagery only, no human figures at all, to avoid any implied ethnic likeness for a real ancient population. Cliffhanger states the paper's own open question truthfully ('is a mystery') rather than inventing an answer -- reserved for Part 5.",
